Z||000003||FieroFanaticus2||05-01-2001||12:09 AM||||Just curious, what are the advantages of having that on your vehicle?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-01-2001||12:26 AM||||You can duct it into the engine. This provides "clean air" (racers term for cooler unobstructed air) I use it to keep the engine compartment cool at present. I am still looking at ducting to the engine (V-6) but the way I'd like to do it needs to be experimented with. Lately I seem to have less time to try different things, But I have seen a car without cruise control and the space I need may be there! (I'd have to lose my Cruise Control, but it's not working anyways)<BR>It is very easy to duct into the engine with a 4-cyl!<BR>Finally, It looks unique!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
